abstract: >
  Full-scale emotion analysis system for 253,886 Spanish economic headlines
  (2014-2024) from 1,436 digital media outlets. Uses RoBERTa-base-bne for
  primary emotion classification into 7 categories (anger, fear, joy, sadness,
  surprise, disgust, others), Gemma 3:4b for cross-validation on 16,651
  non-neutral headlines, and ARIMAX/VAR models for econometric analysis of
  the relationship between media sentiment and macroeconomic indicators
  (CPI, Consumer Confidence Index, Social Security affiliations). Includes
  Granger causality testing, impulse-response functions, and structural
  break detection around the COVID-19 pandemic.
